kivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou","names":{"fr":"Mosquée Zongo de Cotonou"},"photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Petite_mosqu%C3%A9e_de_Zongo_02.jpg/1280px-Petite_mosqu%C3%A9e_de_Zongo_02.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Petite_mosqu%C3%A9e_de_Zongo_02.jpg/500px-Petite_mosqu%C3%A9e_de_Zongo_02.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Richmond Dakpogan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petite_mosqu%C3%A9e_de_Zongo_02.jpg"}},{"id":"cotonou_fondation_zinsou","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Fondation Zinsou","category":"gallery","tags":["art","museums"],"location":{"lat":6.35172,"lng":2.37275},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"cotonou_fondation_zinsou","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://fondationzinsou.org/","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":3,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["fondationzinsou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"13:00","close":"19:00"},{"open":"08:30","close":"19:00"},{"open":"08:30","close":"19:00"},{"open":"08:30","close":"19:00"},{"open":"08:30","close":"19:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"},null],"note":"Closed Sun"},"summary":"Run by one of Benin's first families (current head Lionel was defeated in a presidential election in 2016), the Fondation Zinsou is devoted to showing contemporary art in Benin and providing supporting arts education for children. Their main Cotonou gallery hosts rotating exhibitions and is probably the best place to snag a peek of contemporary Beninese art, though the Fondation also exhibits inte","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/Fondation_Zinsou_in_Cotonou_2015.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/Fondation_Zinsou_in_Cotonou_2015.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"David Stanley from Nanaimo, Canada","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fondation_Zinsou_in_Cotonou_2015.jpg"}},{"id":"cotonou_wv_airplane_on_the_beach","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Airplane on the beach","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":6.34765,"lng":2.37977},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_airplane_on_the_beach","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":4,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["airplaneonthebeach","cotonou"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"You can enter this old Lockheed L-1011 Tristar which the owner has parked on the beach","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_monument_bio_guera","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Monument Bio Guera","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":6.35004,"lng":2.38754},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_monument_bio_guera","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":1,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["monumentbioguera","cotonou"],"summary":"Statue in tribute to resistance fighter Bio Guera on horseback in a charge against the French colonialists.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Monument_de_Bio_Guera_%C3%A0_Cotonou.jpg/1280px-Monument_de_Bio_Guera_%C3%A0_Cotonou.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Monument_de_Bio_Guera_%C3%A0_Cotonou.jpg/500px-Monument_de_Bio_Guera_%C3%A0_Cotonou.jpg","w":1200,"h":1600,"author":"Yendifa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monument_de_Bio_Guera_%C3%A0_Cotonou.jpg"}},{"id":"cotonou_wv_air_de_jeux_plage_erevan","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Air de Jeux Plage Erevan","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":6.34786,"lng":2.37849},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_air_de_jeux_plage_erevan","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":1,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["airdejeuxplageerevan","cotonou"],"summary":"Interesting stretch in that you have an Airbus A300 parked in the sand behind you. May be a little dirty. Just west of here is an extensive beach called Fidjrosse Beach (Plage De Fidjrosse). With both of these, watch out for powerful surf and don't go after dark.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_obama_beach","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Obama Beach","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":6.3438,"lng":2.40315},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_obama_beach","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["obamabeach","cotonou"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Another beach with the well-known namesake and even a sign of him if you want a photo op. This beach is a little dirtier than the other, and also subject to strong surf and security considerations.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_drink_city","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Drink City","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":6.3854,"lng":2.3811},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_drink_city","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["drinkcity","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"There are innumerable buvettes in the complex surrounding Stade de l'Amitié, so you really can't go wrong, but a good choice is Drink City - chiefly due to the beer on tap that is available. There are even rumours that they have had Guinness on tap, a real rarity, in addition to the more common Castel. Rotisserie chicken and grilled fish are on hand for the hungry.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_cafe_fondation_zinsou","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Café Fondation Zinsou","category":"cafe","tags":["cafes"],"location":{"lat":6.3638,"lng":2.4193},"visitMinutes":45,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_cafe_fondation_zinsou","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://fondationzinsou.org/le-cafe-cotonou/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["cafefondationzinsou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Cotonou is very short on the type of coffee shops where hipsters congregate to bury their nose in their laptops. This is the closest thing to it, and probably the only place you can find iced coffee. The colonial undertones are wack, but they always have a rad collection of African tunes and books for sale. Also does a happy-hour on Fridays from 18:00-21:00.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_mad_lounge","areaId":"cotonou","name":"MAD Lounge","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":6.3569,"lng":2.3896},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_mad_lounge","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["madlounge","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"09:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"09:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"09:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"09:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"09:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"09:00","close":"23:59"}]},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Tucked away at the end of the Haie Vive strip, MAD Lounge is a hookah bar popular with twentysomethings, who come dressed to impress. It's the kind of place that has Trace Urban on at a good volume, but still feels relaxing thanks to the airy, thatched-roof setup and comfortably plush furniture. Good spot to start out before a night of dancing.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_shamiana","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Shamiana","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3544,"lng":2.3988},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_shamiana","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["shamianacotonou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"11:30","close":"23:30"},{"open":"11:30","close":"23:30"},{"open":"11:30","close":"23:30"},{"open":"11:30","close":"23:30"},{"open":"11:30","close":"23:30"},{"open":"11:30","close":"23:30"},{"open":"11:30","close":"23:30"}]},"summary":"Probably the best restaurant in Cotonou. Serves up a wide variety of Indian dishes from across the subcontinent, and has a few Chinese-style dishes as well. Good luck finding a nicer, more engaging person to take your order than the guy who runs this place: he's a gem who will make certain you have as much or as little spice as you want.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_code_bar","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Code Bar","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":6.3517,"lng":2.3868},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_code_bar","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["codebar","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},null,null,{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Closed Fri, Sat"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Code Bar has been the trendiest spot for both locals and visitors to party since it opened. It's not quite a club, more an open-air layout and lounge-y cabanas. Plenty imbibe the bottle service or cocktails and take a turn on the dance floor to the blend of African and hip-hop beats. Also hosts a popular Thursday happy-hour BBQ.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_rousski_dom","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Rousski Dom","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3545,"lng":2.3991},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":3,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_rousski_dom","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["rousskidom","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"23:00"}]},"summary":"As a former Marxist-Leninst state, Benin cultivated ties with Mother Russia - sending students for cultural exchanges and building Stalinist monuments around town. Those days are gone, but Slavic gastronomy still survives in the form of this swank outpost, which also boasts a well-stocked vodka bar.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_africa_sound_city","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Africa Sound City","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":6.3928,"lng":2.3649},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_africa_sound_city","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://www.facebook.com/pages/Africa-Sound-City-Kindonou/146835475763662","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["africasoundcity","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Probably Cotonou's foremost live music venue. It's not very big, but there is a good-sized, professional-looking stage in the back, and a bar stacked with cases of beer in the front. Has an eclectic roster of bookings. The kind of place with Fela Kuti and Thomas Sankara portraits on the walls.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_chez_maman_benin","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Chez Maman Bénin","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3625,"lng":2.4227},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_chez_maman_benin","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["chezmamanbenin","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"}]},"summary":"A local institution that's been running for several decades. This is not the very best Beninese food you will eat, but it's a great introduction: they have an ample selection of dishes and an indoor dining room, both of which are far from the norm at low-end restaurants and maquis here.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_fifadji_pork_maquis","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Fifadji Pork Maquis","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.391,"lng":2.3939},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_fifadji_pork_maquis","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["fifadjiporkmaquis","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"18:00"}]},"summary":"This maquis does not have a name, but you'll know you're there when you see a grillmaster tending to meats cooked over a grill made from an oil drum. This is the best place in Cotonou to score grilled pork or \"hanlan\", more traditionally associated with Porto-Novo.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_djunta","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Djunta","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":6.3496,"lng":2.3642},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_djunta","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["djuntacotonou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Most come for live music on Friday nights, when the house band plays afrobeat, jazz and even 1950s rock-and-roll until the wee hours. But it's good to drop by any night of the week for a cheap beer right on the beach under the glow of the Christmas-kitsch lights.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_ci_gusta","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Ci'gusta","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3554,"lng":2.4174},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_ci_gusta","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.cigusta.com","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["cigustacotonou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"}]},"summary":"Cotonou outpost of a chain that serves Italian-style ice cream, paninis and pizza across the Global South, Ci'gusta rapidly became the city's top spot for ice cream upon its opening. A welcome respite from the equatorial sun, though it does get crowded.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_la_galette_a_sucre","areaId":"cotonou","name":"La Galette à Sucre","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3539,"lng":2.3976},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_la_galette_a_sucre","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["lagaletteasucre","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"23:00"}]},"summary":"A bakery and brunch spot that's always packed. Offers a range of breads and pastries, often using locally-sourced products (some of which are also sold here). Affordable crêpes, omelettes and sandwiches are available if you want to sit in.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_mandarine","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Mandarine","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3539,"lng":2.3958},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_mandarine","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["mandarinecotonou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"11:00","close":"23:59"}]},"summary":"An incredible spot for Lebanese food, with a significant Lebanese clientele. Fantastic hummus, baba ghanouj, and other Lebanese specialities, fresh-baked bread, perfectly grilled meats and more at reasonable prices. Note no alcohol served.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_pili_pili","areaId":"cotonou","name":"Pili-Pili","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3597,"lng":2.4231},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_pili_pili","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["pilipilicotonou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"19:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"19:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"19:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"19:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"19:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"19:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"19:00","close":"23:30"}]},"summary":"Pili serves classic grilled meats: chicken, guinea fowl (a bigger, uglier, tastier chicken), beef and fish - all with a liberal helping of piment on the side. There are salads, side dishes and wines, but that's not why you're here.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"},{"id":"cotonou_wv_l_aubergeade","areaId":"cotonou","name":"L'Aubergeade","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":6.3594,"lng":2.4328},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"cotonou_wv_l_aubergeade","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["laubergeadecotonou","cotonou"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"A French-run restaurant with spiffy throwback décor, L'Aubergeade serves African and European fare in large portions, especially grilled meat and fish. There's also a smart cocktail menu here - overall, great value for your franc.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Cotonou"}],"sources":["Wikidata (CC0)","Wikimedia Commons (counts; photos credited per file)","Wikipedia (pageviews; summaries CC BY-SA 4.0)","Wikivoyage (listings: hours, prices, descriptions; CC BY-SA 4.0)","OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL): opening hours, fees, websites"]}